course: dictionary
lesson: 9571
title: Stranger and strange
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stranger is a person you do not know. Context tells you which meaning is meant. «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» The sentence is about people you do not know, so it is a warning not to carry things for them.
explain: Stranger can also mean a person who is new to a place. «I'm a stranger here» means the speaker has never been to this place before. Read the words around it to be sure: if someone says they are new, the meaning is about place, not about people they have never met.
explain: Stranger is also the comparative of strange, which means more unusual. «The story got stranger and stranger.» Swap in more unusual and it still makes sense: the story got more and more unusual. That swap is a good check.
fact: A stranger is a person you do not know.
fact: «Stranger» can also mean someone new to a place, as in «I'm a stranger here».
fact: «Stranger» is also the comparative of «strange», meaning more unusual.
fact: Most strangers are kind, but you do not go anywhere with a stranger, or take things from them, without a trusted adult saying it is okay.
fact: If a stranger makes you feel uncomfortable, say no, get away and tell an adult straight away.
exercise: «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» What is a stranger? | A pet that visits | A teacher you see every day | *A person you do not know | A family member
exercise: «The story got stranger and stranger.» Here stranger means | Lost in the woods | *More and more unusual | A person who is new to a place | Very loud
exercise: If a stranger makes you feel uncomfortable, what should you do? | Take something from them | *Say no, get away and tell an adult | Keep it secret and wait for them | Go with them to see where they live
test: «I'm a stranger here.» What does stranger mean in this sentence? | A very strange animal | A kind shopkeeper who knows you | Someone who is famous | *A person who is new to this place
test: If you are lost, which person is a safe stranger to ask for help? | A stranger who asks for your address | A stranger who offers you a lift | A person messaging you privately online | *A police officer or a shop worker at the till
exam: «Viruses are stranger still: they cannot do anything on their own.» What does stranger mean here? | *More unusual or surprising | Pushed out of the way | Smaller and weaker | Closer and friendlier
